Auth fixture check: Compatible recovery fragment is cleared before boot, stays outside DOM/storage and validates once only after explicit confirmation
Auth fixture check: Cancelling offered navigation before validation destroys hash without consuming provider token or resurrecting it on reopen
Auth fixture check: Bearer/refresh navigation remains discarded and never becomes signed-in or recovery context
Auth fixture check: Recovery email request is explicit, email-only and gives conditional delivery/account wording without authenticating or retaining recipient
Auth fixture check: Closing during an email request waits, clears recipient, never repeats mail or claims to retract delivery, and performs no fake logout
Auth fixture check: Provider captcha/refusal remains sanitized with no existence claim, configuration bypass or automatic resend
Auth fixture check: Recovery link yields password-only context with no workspace/business access, clears secrets and requires fresh login after update
Auth fixture check: Recovery requires owned TOTP before password entry and cancellation neither updates password nor resets the factor
Auth fixture check: Cancelled recovery waits for late credential cleanup and never installs a signed-in workspace or hidden secret
Auth fixture check: Additional TOTP under AAL2 uses distinct manual label, retains verified factor and requires fresh login after confirmation
Auth fixture check: Additional setup resumes live pending TOTP after AAL2 without issuing another enrollment or returning its old seed
Auth fixture check: Additional setup without verified factor gives first-enrollment guidance and preserves the current authenticated session
Auth fixture check: Own security panel displays live confirmed/pending factors and advisory AAL without secrets, contact data or writes
Auth fixture check: Failed security update removes the old snapshot and preserves the authenticated session for explicit retry
Auth fixture check: Closing own security during a held read cannot repopulate hidden private DOM with the late response
Auth fixture check: Explicit first TOTP setup renders local provisioning, confirms once and clears secrets before new login
Auth fixture check: New TOTP QR is rendered in local canvas without URI/seed attributes and raster is erased on confirmation
Auth fixture check: Unavailable canvas preserves the manual key with clear guidance, no second enrollment and no leftover raster
Auth fixture check: Owned pending TOTP resumes confirmation without creating another factor or redisplaying the old key
Auth fixture check: Cancellation before setup preserves the draft; after setup it removes local secrets, reports pending factor and logs out without deletion
Auth fixture check: Human entry waits for configured Auth transport instead of submitting the native form during startup
Auth fixture check: Verified TOTP is required before workspace discovery; wrong code stays blocked and explicit retry completes login
Auth fixture check: Cancellation during TOTP verification waits for the newest credential and never installs it
Auth fixture check: Server MFA requirement after login clears the prior workspace and requires a new authenticated entry
Auth fixture check: Explicit code request serializes with password change, clears secrets and sends nonce once without business replay
Auth fixture check: Unconfirmed code request preserves the current context and never retries or mutates the password
Auth fixture check: Invalid nonce is refused explicitly without provider diagnostics or automatic code/password resend
Auth fixture check: Password confirmation mismatch and cancellation dispatch no change and clear password inputs
Auth fixture check: Confirmed password change sends once with fields cleared and requires new login without business replay
Auth fixture check: Password response loss stays unconfirmed without retry and reports unconfirmed logout
Auth fixture check: Password change respects MFA refusal
Auth fixture check: Cancelling global logout preserves the current draft and contacts no provider
Auth fixture check: Confirmed global logout clears the DOM immediately and blocks new login while revocation is pending
Auth fixture check: Failed global logout before service release clears local identity and reports unconfirmed revocation
Auth fixture check: Cancelling workspace change preserves the current session and draft
Auth fixture check: Confirmed workspace change removes old context and requires new authentication and workspace discovery
Auth fixture check: Workspace change before service release preserves honest reporting of unconfirmed provider logout
Auth fixture check: Workspace change refuses an in-flight mutation without clearing its draft or replaying the request
Auth fixture check: Human page logs in through validated session with password cleared and no persistent token storage
Auth fixture check: List refresh renews the human access token without erasing the active draft
Auth fixture check: Paused refresh preserves the draft, dispatches no mutation, and requires explicit resubmission after resume
Auth fixture check: Unconfirmed provider logout removes local ticket/draft immediately and reports the limitation
Auth fixture check: Cancelled login never shows the application and closes the late-returned synthetic provider session
Auth fixture check: Authentication-only login validates own profile without requesting business data or displaying an empty ticket list
Auth fixture check: Authentication-only signed-in page allows explicit provider logout and a new login
Auth fixture check: Login discovers a single authorized workspace without entering its UUID and then validates selected /me
Auth fixture check: Multiple authorized workspaces require explicit selection before any /me or business request
Auth fixture check: Cancel during workspace choice closes the provider session without confirming a workspace
Auth fixture check: A workspace revoked after discovery fails /me and closes the inaccessible human session
